            <link>https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/hbcus-enter-new-fight-for-equal-funding</link>
            <description><![CDATA[A lawsuit in Missouri could have implications for the nation's historically Black colleges and universities. Current and former students at Lincoln University are suing the state for $549 million, alleging it systematically underfunded the school. The case could become a model for similar legal challenges across the country. Geoff Bennett spoke with Don Calloway for our series, Rethinking College.]]></description>
